From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] u_vbuf: release the retired uploader buffers of each draw of a multi-draw

u_vbuf_draw_vbo hands the uploader's retired buffers back to its caller, so that they outlive the draw that last
used them: a single slot for a translated draw (u_vbuf_translate_begin) and an array for uploaded user buffers
(u_vbuf_upload_buffers, which writes it from its first element and sets the count). They were released once, after
the last draw. A multi-draw takes the loop once per draw, so each draw wrote over the previous draw's slot and
array: a buffer the uploader retired in an earlier draw was never released, and a client-array game that draws many
pieces in one call (a block-building game with a mod renderer) ran the GPU out of buffers. Each draw now releases what it was
given once the driver has taken its own references, before the next draw.

The problem was found by reading ProsperoMC (Ayoubec/ProsperoMC, GPL-3.0; commit 03e6e27, its
scripts/fix-mesa-upload-lifetime.py); this change is written independently here (PS5_Proton NOTICE.md,
"prospero-win and ProsperoMC"). Not run on a console.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_vbuf.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_vbuf.c
index 882f683..b9b6df1 100644
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_vbuf.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_vbuf.c
@@ -1761,6 +1761,15 @@ void u_vbuf_draw_vbo(struct pipe_context *pipe, const struct pipe_draw_info *inf
          pipe->draw_vbo(pipe, &new_info, drawid_offset, indirect, &new_draw, 1);
       if (info->increment_draw_id)
          drawid_offset++;
+
+      /* The driver holds its own references to what this draw bound, so the retired uploader buffers it was handed can
+       * go now. Kept to the end of the call, the next draw of a multi-draw would write over them (a translated draw's
+       * single slot, an upload's array from its first element) and the buffers would never be released. */
+      pipe_resource_release(pipe, releasebuf);
+      releasebuf = NULL;
+      for (unsigned i = 0; i < release_count; i++)
+         pipe_resource_release(pipe, releasebufs[i]);
+      release_count = 0;
    }
 
    if (mgr->using_translate) {
